  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the scene as the experiencer of the metaphorical 'shower'",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the scene (dimly_lit_underground_shower) as the individual who has undergone or is undergoing the metaphorical 'shower' — a necessary but undeserved hardship. The text 'not the shower we deserved but the shower we needed' uses the first-person plural 'we', which creates an inclusive projection where the viewer/user identifies with the collective experience. The scene visually embodies the 'shower' as a grim, necessary cleansing, and the user is projected onto this scene as the one who must endure it. This projection is not explicit with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but it is implied through the collective 'we' and the universalizing tone of the message, making the user feel personally connected to the experience.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
